  "summary_en": "Bulgarian version of the European Parliament's 2017 resolution recommending that the Commission propose EU civil law rules on robotics. It covers definitions, registration, liability, mandatory insurance and compensation funds, an EU robotics agency, ethics, standards, autonomous vehicles, drones, care and medical robots, and employment. It annexes an ethical Charter on Robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Calls for common EU definitions of smart autonomous robots and an EU-wide registration system for advanced robots",
   "Asks the Commission to consider an EU Agency for Robotics and AI",
   "Proposes strict liability or risk-management approach, mandatory insurance and a compensation fund; raises a long-term 'electronic person' status",
   "Annexes a voluntary Charter on Robotics with a code of conduct for engineers, a code for research ethics committees, and licences for designers and users",
   "Requires transparency, a 'black box', kill switches, privacy by design, and no weaponisation of robots"
  ],
